  "notes": [
   "The tutorial says 'any MKR family board'; arduino-mkr-wifi-1010 was chosen as a representative board. Its pins 1, 2, 3, 4 and GND are assumed to plug into the shield's matching header sockets.",
   "The MKR Relay Shield is not in the catalogue, so it is a new part type. Relay 1 is wired internally to pin 1 and relay 2 to pin 2. The relay coil/contact switching (COM to NO/NC) and the other pass-through header pins are not modelled.",
   "The circuit images for the optional LED circuit (IMG05) were not provided. I assumed this layout: pin 3 -> 220 ohm resistor -> LED 1 -> GND, and pin 4 -> 220 ohm resistor -> LED 2 -> GND. The resistor value (220) and the breadboard hole positions are assumptions.",
   "The jumper wires are attached to the MKR board's pins 3, 4 and GND, which are the same nets as the shield's header sockets.",
   "The 24V power supply and 24V lamp example on the relay screw terminals (IMG07) is described only as an illustration, and no image was provided, so it is not part of the graph.",
   "The relay coil power connections on the shield are internal and not modelled."
  ]
